msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/name-drop-signpost.md:11
msgid ""
"/// A parsed representation of a [MARC 21 record leader][leader].\n"
"///\n"
"/// A MARC leader contains metadata that dictates how to interpret the "
"rest  \n"
"/// of the record.\n"
"///\n"
"/// [leader]: https://www.loc.gov/marc/bibliographic/bdleader.html\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/name-drop-signpost.md:19
msgid ""
"/// Determines the schema and the set of valid subsequent data fields.  \n"
"    ///\n"
"    /// Encoded in byte 6 of the leader.  \n"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/name-drop-signpost.md:24
msgid ""
"/// Indicates whether to parse relationship fields, such as a \"773 Host  \n"
"    /// Item Entry\" for an article within a larger work.  \n"
"    ///  \n"
"    /// Encoded in byte 7 of the leader.  \n"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/name-drop-signpost.md:29
msgid "// ... other fields\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/name-drop-signpost.md:31
msgid ""
"/// Parses the [leader of a MARC 21 record][leader].\n"
"///  \n"
"/// The leader is encoded as a fixed-length 24-byte field, containing "
"metadata  \n"
"/// that determines the semantic interpretation of the rest of the "
"record.  \n"
"/// \n"
"/// [leader]: https://www.loc.gov/marc/bibliographic/bdleader.html\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/name-drop-signpost.md:48
msgid ""
"Motivation: Readers of documentation will not be closely reading most of "
"your doc comments like they would dialogue in a novel they love."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/name-drop-signpost.md:51
msgid ""
"Users will most likely be skimming and scan-reading to find the part of the "
"documentation that is relevant to whatever problem they're trying to solve "
"in the moment."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/name-drop-signpost.md:55
msgid ""
"Once a user has found a keyword or potential signpost that's relevant to "
"them they will begin to search for context surrounding what is being "
"documented."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/name-drop-signpost.md:58
msgid ""
"Ask the class: What do you look for in documentation? Focus on the moment-to-"
"moment searching for information here, not general values in documentation."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/name-drop-signpost.md:62
msgid "Name-drop keywords close to the beginning of a paragraph."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/name-drop-signpost.md:64
msgid ""
"This aids skimming and scanning, as the first few words of a paragraph stand "
"out the most."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/name-drop-signpost.md:67
msgid ""
"Skimming and scanning lets users quickly navigate a text, keeping keywords "
"as close to the beginning of a paragraph as possible lets a user determine "
"if they've found relevant information faster."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/name-drop-signpost.md:71
msgid "Signpost, but don't over-explain."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/name-drop-signpost.md:73
msgid ""
"Users will not necessarily have the same domain expertise as an API designer."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/name-drop-signpost.md:75
msgid ""
"If a tangential, specialist term or acronym is mentioned try to bring in "
"enough context such that a novice could quickly do more research."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/name-drop-signpost.md:78
msgid ""
"Signposting often happens organically, consider a networking library that "
"mentions various protocols. But when it doesn't happen organically, it can "
"be difficult to choose what to mention."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/name-drop-signpost.md:82
msgid ""
"Rule of thumb: API developers should be asking themselves \"if a novice ran "
"into what they are documenting, what sources would they look up and are "
"there any red herrings they might end up following\"?"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/name-drop-signpost.md:86
msgid ""
"Users should be given enough information to look up subjects on their own."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/meaningful-doc-comments/name-drop-signpost.md:88
msgid ""
"What we've already covered, predictability of an API including the naming "
"conventions, is a form of signposting."
msgstr ""
